config BR2_PACKAGE_IOEXAMPLE6
    bool "Example6: PWM Interactive Demo (TIM3_CH1, PB4)"
    select BR2_PACKAGE_PERIPHERY
    help
      This package provides a simple utility demonstrating the usage of
      the Linux PWM sysfs interface on an STM32F4-based board.

      It enables PWM output on chip0, channel0 (TIM3_CH1, PB4). The user can
      enter any integer duty cycle from 0 to 100 percent, or q to quit.

      Connect an external LED in series with a 330-680 ohm resistor between
      PB4 and GND. The onboard LEDs on PG13 and PG14 do not expose timer PWM
      alternate functions on STM32F429.

      The example shows:
        - Opening and configuring a PWM channel
        - Setting frequency and duty cycle
        - Enabling/disabling PWM output
        - Basic user interaction for testing LED brightness or signal levels

      Dependencies:
        https://github.com/vsergeev/c-periphery
